From: Zetarancio <zetarancio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Mar 2026 23:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] miyoo-serial: improved joystick with frame sync, report
 threshold, miyoo-* DTS properties

Improvements to the Miyoo serial joystick path, closely matching
the stock miyoo_inputd behaviour:

1. Simple radial deadzone (no remapping):
   Zero values inside the deadzone without rescaling the output
   range.  The previous remapping formula amplified quantisation
   noise from the 8-bit MCU ADC near the deadzone boundary.

2. Report threshold (miyoo-threshold DTS property, default 128):
   Only update a reported axis value when the change from the last
   report exceeds the threshold.  Stock miyoo_inputd uses
   TRIMUI_AXIS_RANGE >> 8 = 128.  Suppresses jitter without
   adding latency.

3. Byte-by-byte frame synchronisation (miyoo_read_frame):
   Auto-recovers from UART desync instead of permanently misaligning
   on partial reads.

4. VMIN=0 / VTIME=1 for non-blocking TTY reads:
   Allows kthread_should_stop() and the inactivity timer to be checked
   periodically, enabling clean shutdown and reliable recovery.

5. Miyoo-specific DTS properties (miyoo-deadzone, miyoo-fuzz,
   miyoo-flat, miyoo-threshold, miyoo-{lx,ly,rx,ry}-{p,n}-tuning).

6. 100 calibration frames (was 50); removed static float deadzone.

Attribution: serial framing, report threshold, and deadzone handling
aligned with the stock Miyoo Flip joystick input path.

DTS properties (Miyoo serial path):
  miyoo-deadzone    absolute deadzone in [-32760..32760] range
  miyoo-fuzz        input fuzz for ABS params
  miyoo-flat        input flat for ABS params
  miyoo-threshold   report change threshold (default 128, 0 = off)
  miyoo-{lx,ly,rx,ry}-{p,n}-tuning   per-axis scaling (100 = unity)
